{"id":"e20bf8829c6e43e01135f04897d6954525ff54d1","axis":"silent","repo":"supabase/supabase","sha":"e20bf8829c6e43e01135f04897d6954525ff54d1","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"apps/docs/content/guides/ai/examples/semantic-image-search-amazon-titan.mdx","lines":["@@ -37,7 +37,7 @@ When creating your project, make sure to note down your database password as you"," You can find your database connection string on your project dashboard, click [Connect](/dashboard/project/_?showConnect=true). Use the Session [pooler](/docs/guides/database/connecting-to-postgres/pooling-and-limits) connection string which looks like this:"," "," ```txt","-postgresql://postgres.[PROJECT-REF]:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@aws-0-[REGION].pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres","+postgresql://postgres.[PROJECT-REF]:[YOUR-DATABASE-PASSWORD]@aws-0-[REGION].pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres"," ```"," "," ## Install the dependencies","@@ -66,7 +66,7 @@ from matplotlib import pyplot as plt"," from matplotlib import image as mpimg"," from typing import Optional"," ","-DB_CONNECTION = \"postgresql://postgres.[PROJECT-REF]:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@aws-0-[REGION].pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres\"","+DB_CONNECTION = \"postgresql://postgres.[PROJECT-REF]:[YOUR-DATABASE-PASSWORD]@aws-0-[REGION].pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres\""," ```"," "," Next, get the [credentials to your AWS account](https://boto3.amazonaws.com/v1/documentation/api/latest/guide/credentials.html) and instantiate the `boto3` client:"],"additions":2,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"apps/docs/content/guides/auth/passwords.mdx","lines":["@@ -8,6 +8,11 @@ Users often expect to sign in to your site with a password. Supabase Auth helps"," "," Users can associate a password with their identity using their [email address](#with-email) or a [phone number](#with-phone)."," ","+<Admonition type=\"warning\" title=\"Reset database password\">","+  Looking for a database password? See [Reset database","+  password](/kb/troubleshooting/how-do-i-reset-my-supabase-database-password-oTs5sB).","+</Admonition>","+"," ## With email"," "," ### Enabling email and password-based authentication"],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"apps/docs/content/guides/database/connecting-to-postgres.mdx","lines":["@@ -44,7 +44,7 @@ For every Postgres connection mode, the string comes from the same place:"," 1. Open your project in the [Supabase Dashboard](/dashboard/project/_)."," 2. Click **Connect** at the top of the page."," 3. Choose the connection method you picked above.","-4. Copy the string and replace `[YOUR-PASSWORD]` with your database password. [Percent-encode](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Percent-encoding) any reserved characters it contains, such as `&`, `#`, `?`, or a space.","+4. Copy the string and replace `[YOUR-DATABASE-PASSWORD]` with your database password. [Percent-encode](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Percent-encoding) any reserved characters it contains, such as `&`, `#`, `?`, or a space."," "," The sections below show what each string looks like and when to use it. Take the host, port, and username from the string you copied rather than typing the bracketed placeholders literally. The pooler host in particular can't be composed from your region, and pooled connections use a different username from direct connections. Both are covered under [Endpoints and IP versions](#endpoints-and-ip-versions)."," ","@@ -59,7 +59,7 @@ Direct connections are on IPv6, or on IPv4 if the project has the [IPv4 add-on]("," </Admonition>"," "," ```txt","-postgresql://postgres:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@db.[PROJECT-REF].supabase.co:5432/postgres","+postgresql://postgres:[YOUR-DATABASE-PASSWORD]@db.[PROJECT-REF].supabase.co:5432/postgres"," ```"," "," Get this string from the Supabase Dashboard by clicking [Connect](/dashboard/project/_?showConnect=true).","@@ -69,7 +69,7 @@ Get this string from the Supabase Dashboard by clicking [Connect](/dashboard/pro"," The session mode connection string connects to your Postgres instance through the shared pooler ([Supavisor](https://supabase.github.io/supavisor/)). Use it as an alternative to a direct connection when you connect from an IPv4-only network."," "," ```txt","-postgresql://postgres.[PROJECT-REF]:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@[POOLER-HOST]:5432/postgres","+postgresql://postgres.[PROJECT-REF]:[YOUR-DATABASE-PASSWORD]@[POOLER-HOST]:5432/postgres"," ```"," "," Get this string from the Supabase Dashboard by clicking [Connect](/dashboard/project/_?showConnect=true&method=session) and choosing **Session pooler**.","@@ -91,7 +91,7 @@ Transaction mode does not support [query pipelining](https://www.postgresql.org/"," </Admonition>"," "," ```txt","-postgresql://postgres.[PROJECT-REF]:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@[POOLER-HOST]:6543/postgres","+postgresql://postgres.[PROJECT-REF]:[YOUR-DATABASE-PASSWORD]@[POOLER-HOST]:6543/postgres"," ```"," "," Get this string from the Supabase Dashboard by clicking [Connect](/dashboard/project/_?showConnect=true&method=transaction) and choosing **Transaction pooler**.","@@ -101,7 +101,7 @@ Get this string from the Supabase Dashboard by clicking [Connect](/dashboard/pro"," On the Pro Plan and above, Supabase provisions a dedicated pooler (PgBouncer) that runs alongside your Postgres database. Use it for high-load applications. The dedicated pooler runs in transaction mode only. For session mode, use the [shared pooler](#pooler-session-mode). Unlike the shared pooler, it supports prepared statements on PgBouncer 1.21 and later. It is reachable over IPv6, or over IPv4 if the project has the [IPv4 add-on](/docs/guides/platform/ipv4-address)."," "," ```txt","-postgresql://postgres:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@db.[PROJECT-REF].supabase.co:6543/postgres","+postgresql://postgres:[YOUR-DATABASE-PASSWORD]@db.[PROJECT-REF].supabase.co:6543/postgres"," ```"," "," Get this string from the Supabase Dashboard by clicking [Connect](/dashboard/project/_?showConnect=true&method=transaction)."],"additions":5,"deletions":5,"truncated":false},{"path":"apps/docs/content/guides/database/connecting-to-postgres/serverless-drivers.mdx","lines":["@@ -53,7 +53,7 @@ Choose one of these Vercel Deploy Templates. They use the [Vercel Deploy Integra"," 4. Save the result as the `POSTGRES_URL` environment variable."," "," ```dotenv .env.local","-POSTGRES_URL=\"postgresql://postgres.[PROJECT-REF]:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@[POOLER-HOST]:6543/postgres?workaround=supabase-pooler.vercel\"","+POSTGRES_URL=\"postgresql://postgres.[PROJECT-REF]:[YOUR-DATABASE-PASSWORD]@[POOLER-HOST]:6543/postgres?workaround=supabase-pooler.vercel\""," ```"," "," <Tabs scrollable defaultActiveId=\"drizzle\" type=\"underlined\" size=\"small\">"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"apps/docs/content/guides/getting-started/quickstarts/laravel.mdx","lines":["@@ -47,7 +47,7 @@ Pass a stack name such as `blade`, `react`, or `vue` when prompted. The example"," "," ```bash name=.env"," DB_CONNECTION=pgsql","-DB_URL=postgres://postgres.[PROJECT-REF]:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@[POOLER-HOST]:5432/postgres","+DB_URL=postgres://postgres.[PROJECT-REF]:[YOUR-DATABASE-PASSWORD]@[POOLER-HOST]:5432/postgres"," ```"," "," Laravel sets `sslmode` as an explicit `config/database.php` option rather than a URL parameter. The next step covers this."],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"apps/docs/content/guides/getting-started/quickstarts/redwoodjs.mdx","lines":["@@ -61,10 +61,10 @@ In your `.env` file, add the following environment variables for your database c"," "," ```bash name=.env"," # Transaction mode connection string for Prisma Client app queries","-DATABASE_URL=\"postgres://postgres.[PROJECT-REF]:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@[POOLER-HOST]:6543/postgres?pgbouncer=true&connection_limit=1\"","+DATABASE_URL=\"postgres://postgres.[PROJECT-REF]:[YOUR-DATABASE-PASSWORD]@[POOLER-HOST]:6543/postgres?pgbouncer=true&connection_limit=1\""," "," # Direct connection string for Prisma Migrate","-DIRECT_URL=\"postgres://postgres:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@db.[PROJECT-REF].supabase.co:5432/postgres\"","+DIRECT_URL=\"postgres: